# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — Project Settings -> API Keys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only the PUBLISHABLE key belongs here. It is safe in a browser because
# row-level security is what actually protects the data.
# NEVER put the secret key in this file.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Maps — https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis/credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enable these APIs on the same Google Cloud project:
#   Maps JavaScript API
#   Directions API   (legacy — the JS DirectionsService still uses this name)
#   Geocoding API
# Directions and Geocoding are how a planned route gets a start, an end, and
# stops placed by kilometres along the drive. Without Directions the console
# still plans a straight line between depot coordinates; the error
# "webpage is not allowed to use the directions service" means the key's
# API restrictions do not include Directions API, or it is not enabled.
#
# This key is visible to anyone who opens the console, which is unavoidable for
# a browser map. Protect it in the Google Cloud console instead:
#   1. Application restrictions -> HTTP referrers, listing only your domains
#      (include http://localhost:5173/* and http://localhost:5175/* for development)
#   2. API restrictions -> Maps JavaScript API, Directions API, Geocoding API
# Without those two restrictions the key can be lifted and billed to you.
#
# The live map falls back to a schematic view when this is empty, so the rest
# of the console works without it.

VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional: a Map ID from Google Cloud, needed for cloud-based map styling.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo sign-in
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Typed into the login form on load, so a store reviewer or anyone being shown
# the console can sign in without being handed credentials separately.
#
# These are NOT a secret: Vite bakes VITE_ variables into the browser bundle,
# so anyone who opens the console can read them. Only ever point them at a demo
# account — never at an account that can see a real customer's fleet.
#
# Leave them empty and the form simply starts blank.

VITE_DEMO_EMAIL=
VITE_DEMO_PASSWORD=
